Creating Networking Resources in an Amazon VPC

Lab Overview

This practical AWS re/Start lab focused on designing and configuring a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) to establish internet connectivity for an EC2 instance.

The lab was based on a customer support scenario in which a startup owner could not successfully ping resources outside their VPC.

Acting as an AWS Cloud Support Engineer, I investigated the networking requirements, created the necessary AWS networking resources and configured the environment to establish outbound internet connectivity.

Duration: Approximately 60 minutes
AWS Services: Amazon VPC, EC2, Internet Gateway, Route Tables, Security Groups and Network ACLs
Operating System: Amazon Linux 2023

Customer Scenario

A startup customer reported that their EC2 instance could not communicate outside their VPC.

The customer had attempted to configure their network but was unable to establish internet connectivity.

The objective was to investigate the configuration, identify missing networking components and implement a solution that would allow the EC2 instance to successfully communicate with the internet.

